.TH imscrbgrmr 1 "May 2026" "Imscribing Grammar" "Imscribing Grammar"
.SH NAME
imscrbgrmr \- 12-primitive structural grammar encoding any system
as a coordinate in a 17,280,000-element Crystal of Types
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBimscribe\fR [\fIcommand\fR] [\fIargs\fR]
\fBuv run crystal_navigator.py\fR {\fBdescribe\fR|\fBgap\fR|\fBverify\fR|\fBrepl\fR|\fBcensus\fR|\fBencode\fR|\fBdecode\fR|\fBnearest\fR|\fBcount\fR} [\fIargs\fR]
\fBpython3 imscribeaudio.py\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR|\fB\-\-tuple\fR \fITUP\fR|\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR|\fB\-\-list\fR] [\fIbase sub\fR]
\fBpython3 imscribevideo.py\fR [\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR|\fB\-\-tuple\fR \fITUP\fR|\fB\-\-all\-catalog\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR]
\fBpython3 esoteric_librarian.py\fR {\fBshow\fR|\fBlist\fR|\fBdist\fR|\fBnear\fR|\fBaudio\fR|\fBvideo\fR|\fBrewrite\fR|\fBscaffold\fR|\fBadd\fR} [\fIargs\fR]
\fBuv run IG_inquiry.py\fR [\fIseed_question\fR] [\fB\-p\fR \fIPROVIDER\fR] [\fB\-m\fR \fIMODEL\fR]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Imscribing Grammar (IG) assigns every system \(em physical, biological,
mathematical, symbolic \(em a 12-tuple of structural primitives placing it in
a discrete space of 17,280,000 structural types (the Crystal of Types).
The grammar classifies its own type; its self-imscribing address is
\fI6,734,591\fR at ouroboricity tier \fIO_inf\fR, the special Frobenius
fixed point where \[mu]\[ci]\[de] = id.
.PP
The 12 primitives are irreducible dimensions:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fBÐ\fR  Dimensionality      \fBÞ\fR  Topology            \fBŘ\fR  Relational mode
\fBΦ\fR  Parity/symmetry     \fBƒ\fR  Fidelity            \fBÇ\fR  Kinetic character
\fBΓ\fR  Scope               \fBɢ\fR  Interaction grammar \fBφ̂\fR  Criticality
\fBĦ\fR  Chirality      \fBΣ\fR  Stoichiometry       \fBΩ\fR  Winding
.fi
.RE
.PP
The Crystal partitions as \fI3^3 \[mu] 4^5 \[mu] 5^4 = 17,280,000\fR types,
organized into 400 tier cells (\fIO_0\fR through \fIO_inf\fR).
.SH QUICK START
.nf
git clone https://github.com/umpolungfish/imscrbgrmr.git
cd imscrbgrmr
uv sync
cp .env.example .env
# edit .env with your provider key
imscribe catalog list
uv run crystal_navigator.py repl
.fi
.SH "IMSCRIBE CLI"
\fBimscribe\fR is the primary CLI for the grammar package.
.TP
\fBimscribe analyze\fR \fINAME\fR
Display the full 12-tuple and primitive breakdown for a named catalog entry.
.TP
\fBimscribe catalog list\fR [\fB\-n\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-offset\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-filter\fR \fISTR\fR]
List catalog entries (default: first 50). Use \fB\-n 0\fR for all.
.TP
\fBimscribe catalog search\fR \fIQUERY\fR
Full-text search across catalog names and descriptions.
.TP
\fBimscribe tool generate\fR
Generate a new imscription via LLM-assisted grammar tool.
.
.SH "CRYSTAL NAVIGATOR"
\fBpython3 crystal_navigator.py\fR implements a bijective Frobenius codec
over the full 17,280,000-type crystal \(em encode any tuple to a unique address
in [0, 17,279,999] and decode back exactly.
.TP
\fBdescribe\fR
Print navigator self-description and crystal statistics.
.TP
\fBgap\fR
Print the tier gap ladder (§69): distances between consecutive ouroboricity tiers.
The Frobenius cliff \fId(O_2dagger, O_inf) ~ 4.382\fR is 3.36x the next-largest gap.
.TP
\fBverify\fR
Verify Frobenius codec roundtrip (encode \(-> decode = identity).
.TP
\fBrepl\fR
Start an interactive navigation REPL for ad-hoc queries.
.TP
\fBcensus\fR
Print full tier census (counts of \fIO_0\fR, \fIO_1\fR, \fIO_2\fR,
\fIO_2dagger\fR, \fIO_inf\fR across all 17.28M types).
.TP
\fBencode\fR \fITUPLE\fR
Encode a 12-primitive tuple to its canonical address.
.TP
\fBdecode\fR \fIADDRESS\fR
Decode a canonical address back to its 12-primitive tuple.
.TP
\fBnearest\fR \fITUPLE\fR
Find the nearest catalog entries to a given tuple.
.TP
\fBcount\fR [\fIconstraints\fR]
Count structural types matching primitive constraints.
.
.SH "AUDIO SYNTHESIS"
\fBpython3 imscribeaudio.py\fR synthesises WAV audio for any individual
symbol, any 12-primitive imscription tuple, or any named catalog entry.
Each primitive value has a canonical phonetic identity encoded as a
(base-glyph, subscript) pair; glyph IDs take the form \fIÐ_ß\fR, \fIφ̂_ÿ\fR, etc.
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Generate the full 49-symbol sequence \(-> \fIimscribing_all_symbols.wav\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-tuple\fR \fITUP\fR
Synthesise a 12-primitive tuple. Glyph IDs may be space- or comma-separated.
Old phonetic names (\fIÐ_omega\fR, \fIÞ_nrleg\fR, etc.) are also accepted.
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR
Synthesise the tuple for a named entry from \fIIG_catalog.json\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-list\fR
Print all 49 canonical glyph IDs.
.TP
\fIbase sub\fR
Synthesise a single symbol (e.g., \fBimscribeaudio.py φ̂ ÿ\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-dur\fR \fIDUR\fR
Duration per symbol in seconds (default: 0.75).
.TP
\fB\-\-fs\fR \fIFS\fR
Sample rate in Hz (default: 44100).
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fIFILE\fR
Output WAV path (default: \fIaudio/<name>.wav\fR).
.PP
The library \fIsounds.py\fR exposes synthesis functions, \fIPRIMITIVE_MAP\fR,
and \fIresolve_id()\fR for programmatic use.
.
.SH "VIDEO RENDERING"
\fBpython3 imscribevideo.py\fR renders a 1280x720 MP4 for any imscription:
one frame per primitive, 12 frames total. As each primitive sounds off, its
glyph lights up and joins the growing chain. Requires \fBffmpeg\fR on \fI$PATH\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR
Render video for a named catalog entry.
.TP
\fB\-\-tuple\fR \fITUP\fR
Render video for a 12-primitive tuple.
.TP
\fB\-\-all\-catalog\fR
Batch render: one video for every catalog entry.
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fIFILE\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR
Output MP4 path (default: \fIaudio/<name>.mp4\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-fps\fR \fIFPS\fR
Frames per second (default: 30).
.TP
\fB\-\-dur\fR \fIDUR\fR
Duration per frame in seconds (default: 0.75).
.TP
\fB\-\-outdir\fR \fIDIR\fR
Output directory for \fI\-\-all\-catalog\fR (default: \fIaudio/\fR).
.
.SH "ESOTERIC LIBRARIAN"
\fBpython3 esoteric_librarian.py\fR navigates imscribed catalogs of
esoteric and philosophical texts at verse/section granularity.
Cross-catalog distance and nearest-neighbor lookup work across the Tao,
Upanishads, Hiss Incantation, and the physics/math catalog.
.TP
\fBshow\fR \fICATALOG\fR \fIKEY\fR
Display full imscription, tier, C_score, text, and notes for an entry.
.TP
\fBlist\fR \fICATALOG\fR [\fB\-\-tier\fR \fIT\fR]
Tabular list of all entries, optionally filtered by criticality tier.
.TP
\fBdist\fR \fICAT_A\fR \fIKEY_A\fR \fICAT_B\fR \fIKEY_B\fR
Hamming distance between two entries (within or across catalogs).
.TP
\fBnear\fR \fICATALOG\fR \fIKEY\fR [\fB\-\-n\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-other\-catalog\fR \fIC\fR]
K nearest neighbors within a catalog, or across a second catalog.
.TP
\fBaudio\fR \fICATALOG\fR \fIKEY\fR [\fB\-\-dur\fR \fID\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR \fIFILE\fR]
Sonify an entry's imscription via imscribeaudio.py.
.TP
\fBvideo\fR \fICATALOG\fR \fIKEY\fR [\fB\-\-dur\fR \fID\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR \fIFILE\fR]
Render an annotated video for an entry via imscribevideo.py.
.TP
\fBrewrite\fR \fICATALOG\fR \fIKEY\fR
Print an address-preserving structural rewrite prompt for the entry.
.TP
\fBscaffold\fR \fICATALOG\fR
Create a ready-to-fill generator script \fIgen_<catalog>.py\fR.
.TP
\fBadd\fR \fICATALOG\fR \fB\-\-tuple\fR \fITUP\fR \fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
Add a single entry to a catalog (creates JSON if absent).
.PP
Catalog short names: \fBtao\fR \(em Tao Te Ching (81 chapters);
\fBig\fR \(em IG_catalog.json (2,600+ systems). Any \fI.json\fR file in
\fIesoteric_library/\fR is resolvable by its basename.
.
.SH "IG INQUIRY AGENT"
\fBuv run IG_inquiry.py\fR runs the open-ended inquiry loop: an agentic
research agent that uses the full grammar toolset (imscribe, distance,
meet/join/tensor, ouroborics, consciousness score) to explore structural
relationships starting from a seed question.
.TP
\fIseed\fR
Seed question or topic (positional argument).
.TP
\fB\-\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR, \fB\-f\fR \fIFILE\fR
Read seed question from a text file.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-catalog\fR
Disable loading \fIIG_catalog.json\fR; start with an empty session catalog.
.TP
\fB\-\-insights\fR
Inject prior-session insights from \fIimscription_insights.json\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-provider\fR \fIPROVIDER\fR, \fB\-p\fR \fIPROVIDER\fR
LLM provider (env: \fIIG_PROVIDER\fR). Supports openrouter, deepseek,
qwen, mistral, gemini, local.
.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fIMODEL\fR, \fB\-m\fR \fIMODEL\fR
Model ID (env: \fIIG_MODEL\fR). Uses provider default if unset.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-iter\fR \fIN\fR, \fB\-n\fR \fIN\fR
Maximum reasoning iterations (env: \fIIG_MAX_ITER\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fIFILE\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR
Export final insights to JSON file (env: \fIIG_OUT\fR).
.PP
Subcommands:
.TP
\fBtool\fR \fINAME\fR [\fIkey=val\fR ...]
Dispatch a grammar tool directly.
.TP
\fBagent\fR \fITASK\fR
Run the \fIO_inf\fR agentic document agent.
.
.SH "DOMAIN NAVIGATORS"
\fBpython3 domain_navigators.py\fR provides cross-domain structural
navigation across Language, Civilization, Ecology, and Consciousness
domains (§74\(en§77).
.TP
\fBinfo\fR [\fB\-\-domain\fR \fIDOM\fR]
Show imscribed primitives for a domain.
.TP
\fBverify\fR [\fB\-\-domain\fR \fIDOM\fR]
Consistency check for a domain's imscribed primitives.
.TP
\fBdistance\fR
Compute structural distance between domain entries.
.TP
\fBnearest\fR
Find nearest domain entries to a given system.
.TP
\fBrepl\fR
Start an interactive domain navigation REPL.
.
.SH "CRYSTAL GNN"
\fBpython3 quiver_crystal.py\fR implements three generations of
quiver-based GNN navigator:
.TP
\fBquiver\fR
49 nodes (one per primitive value), 255 edges including inter-lane
structural correlations (\fIφ̂ <-> Φ\fR, \fIφ̂ <-> Ç\fR, \fIΩ <-> Ð\fR).
.TP
\fBv10 CF-GNN\fR
Crystal-Factored: three family heads (\fIF_3\fR/\fIF_4\fR/\fIF_5\fR) +
\fIFamilyMixer\fR broadcast attention. Composed address error 0.000%.
.TP
\fBv11\fR
Exact self-imscribing from epoch 20, stable for 480+ consecutive epochs.
Self-imscribe error = 0.
.TP
\fBtrain\fR, \fBtrain-v10\fR, \fBtrain-v11\fR
Train the respective model on \fIIG_catalog.json\fR.
.TP
\fBverify\fR, \fBverify-v10\fR, \fBverify-v11\fR
Verify codec quality on catalog sample.
.TP
\fBinfo\fR
Print model architecture and quiver stats.
.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fIIG_catalog.json\fR
2,600+ imscribed systems (source of truth).
.TP
\fIcrystal_navigator.py\fR
Frobenius codec + tier gap ladder + REPL.
.TP
\fIsounds.py\fR
Phonetic synthesis library (49 symbols, PRIMITIVE_MAP).
.TP
\fIimscribeaudio.py\fR
Audio CLI: --tuple, --name, --all, single-symbol.
.TP
\fIimscribevideo.py\fR
Video CLI: annotated MP4 per imscription (1280x720, ffmpeg).
.TP
\fIesoteric_librarian.py\fR
Esoteric library navigator: show/list/dist/near/audio/video/rewrite.
.TP
\fIesoteric_library/\fR
Imscribed esoteric texts (Tao Te Ching, etc.).
.TP
\fIquiver_crystal.py\fR
CrystalGNN: quiver-based neural navigator.
.TP
\fIdomain_navigators.py\fR
Language, civilization, ecology, consciousness navigators.
.TP
\fIIG_inquiry.py\fR
Agent loop: imscribe, distance, meet/join/tensor, ouroborics.
.TP
\fIMAIN_DOCS/\fR
Formal theorems, predictions, ontology, and crystal enumeration.
.TP
\fIimscrbgrmr/\fR
CLI package (imscribe command).
.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Self-describe the Crystal
uv run crystal_navigator.py describe

# Explore the Crystal interactively
uv run crystal_navigator.py repl

# Encode a tuple to an address
uv run crystal_navigator.py encode "Ð_ω Þ_O Ř_Ť Φ_} ƒ_ż Ç_@ Γ_ʔ ɢ_Ş φ̂_ÿ Ħ_! Σ_ï Ω_z"

# Decode address 6734591 back to tuple
uv run crystal_navigator.py decode 6734591

# List first 50 catalog entries
imscribe catalog list

# Analyze a named entry
imscribe analyze riemann_hypothesis

# Full phonetic sequence
python3 imscribeaudio.py --all

# Audio for a named system
python3 imscribeaudio.py --name psychedelic_baseline

# Video for a named system
python3 imscribevideo.py --name riemann_hypothesis

# Tao Te Ching chapter 1
python3 esoteric_librarian.py show tao 1

# Structural distance between chapters
python3 esoteric_librarian.py dist tao 1 tao 81

# Cross-catalog nearest neighbors
python3 esoteric_librarian.py near tao 1 --n 5 --other-catalog ig

# Start inquiry on a topic
uv run IG_inquiry.py "What is the structural type of a magnetar?"
.fi
.
